  "model_card": {
    "summary": "Final synthetic lexical-RAG/address-reading TinyLM.",
    "scope": "Measure generated ASCII address reading and citation with fixed model weights under absent, correct, lexically retrieved, distractor and paired address/source-ID contexts; include the same model's in-context mapping comparison.",
    "limitations": [
      "Generated answers are measured in a small ASCII address world; this is not natural-language RAG competence.",
      "Citation support checks one affirmative address field, not general entailment or source trust.",
      "UNKNOWN is the supervised answer when the requested fact is absent; fact accuracy is reported separately.",
      "The lexical query alias changes are deliberate misses, not model failures.",
      "Paired context interventions change only the held-out announcement address or citation ID; weights and saved splits remain fixed.",
      "These selected branches initialize fresh models in their actual code; a plan-level sft dependency is not evidence of using SFT or UltraChat weights.",
      "The saved language checkpoint performs the document-reading part. The provided infer.py example supplies a document directly; the external lexical retriever and source-ID mapping are separate from model weights. Training includes both generated RAG conversations and the reported in-context mapping conversations.",
      "The ICL comparison contains only one held-out mapping value: zero-shot correctly returns UNKNOWN (1/1), while few-shot, changed and reversed example conditions each score 0/1. This run supplies no successful example-based adaptation evidence.",
      "Correct context scores 5/12 fact answers; adding the distractor scores 2/12 although all 12 citations name a present source. Source-ID validity alone does not establish a correct or supported answer.",
      "The support metric checks a matching address field in the cited document without checking its key against the requested key. In distractor-only context it reports 5/12 support but 0/12 fact answers; it is not a query-entailment test.",
      "Retrieved-context exact match is 6/12, comprising 3 correct fact answers and 3 correct UNKNOWN responses to deliberate retrieval misses; lexical recall@1 is 9/12. Paired baseline-and-change correctness is 5/12 for changed addresses and 2/12 for changed citation IDs."
    ],
